      "writtenOn": "2025-02-26T21:42:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I think the space calculations are wrong in a bunch of places...\n\n\nThe uio needs to hold the terminating FALSE and the EOF marker\n\nSo we need to make sure those will fit, but we also need to make sure we don\u0027t double account for anything...\n\nIn some sense, it might make sense for tracker-\u003emem_avail to not account for those, though the xdr_mem be created with space for them. Then when the FSAL readdir call is done (and thus as many entries as will fit in the tracker-\u003emem_avail space are in the xdr_mem), then the main readdir function just encodes the FALSE for entry termination and the EOF into the xdr_mem using the space it reserved by telling tracker 8 bytes less.",
      "revId": "f072d35ffec5814dc491d5e83238e2929713f7a2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
